refers to a typical or common use of that class of product, regardless
of the status of the particular user or of the way in which the particular
user actually uses, or expects or is expected to use, the product.

  A product is a "consumer product" if the ordinary use of the product
is for personal, family, or household purposes, regardless of whether
the product is ordinarily used in a commercial or industrial setting,
or whether it is ordinarily used in a commercial or industrial setting,
or whether the product has significant non-consumer uses, as far as the
product's ordinary use is concerned.  The determination whether a
product is a consumer product is made on a case-by-case basis, but
regardless of whether a product has significant non-consumer uses, a
product is a consumer product if the ordinary use of the product
is for personal, family or household purposes.  A product is a consumer
product regardless of whether the product has substantial commercial,
industrial or non-consumer uses, unless such uses represent the only
significant mode of use of the product.

